From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:44:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Use the CPU operating
 points

Include the CPU operating points on the Cubie A7S, set them on all
eight CPUs and give the first CPU of each cluster its supply: DCDC5 for
the Cortex-A55 cores and DCDC3 for the Cortex-A76 cores. The other CPUs
of a cluster share the table, and with it the regulator.

The AXP318W settles an output at 10 mV per 7.8125 us, 1280 uV/us, with
its dynamic voltage scaling bit set, and the regulator driver has no
ramp setting of its own; the boot firmware sets the scaling bit and
the kernel does not. Set regulator-ramp-delay on both rails so that
the regulator core waits for the output before the OPP core raises the
clock. The property only sets this wait and programs nothing. A change over
the full 250 mV window waits 196 us.

With this patch cpufreq runs on the Cubie A7S. A kernel without the
sun50i-cpufreq-nvmem support for the A733 finds operating points that
all carry opp-supported-hw and stops with an empty table, so the CPUs
stay at the boot clock.

Not covered: the settling time of a rail with a different slew setting
(the wait is then too short by the factor of the setting) and changing
the AXP318W regulator driver to set the slew.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; cpufreq runs on all
eight CPUs with DCDC5 supplying the A55 cluster and DCDC3 the A76
cluster, each rail follows the operating point of its cluster, holds it
under load at the top points and returns to the lowest voltage at the
lowest points, and no regulator warning or failed voltage setting
appears.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 76793d350b30..e76f308e21ba 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include "sun60i-a733.dtsi"
+#include "sun60i-a733-cpu-opp.dtsi"
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
@@ -90,6 +91,40 @@ combophy0_ss: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+	cpu-supply = <&reg_dcdc5>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster0_opp>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster1_opp>;
+	cpu-supply = <&reg_dcdc3>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&cluster1_opp>;
+};
+
 &ehci1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -224,6 +259,7 @@ reg_dcdc3: dcdc3 {
 				regulator-name = "vdd-cpub";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1050000>;
+				regulator-ramp-delay = <1280>;
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
@@ -240,6 +276,7 @@ reg_dcdc5: dcdc5 {
 				regulator-name = "vdd-cpul";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1050000>;
+				regulator-ramp-delay = <1280>;
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 		};
